description:
When EventSource state event arrives with Chat changes before fetchChats() completes, chatState is null. Handler at line 540 silently skips Chat/changes (no token sync). Compare to Message handler (lines 532-536) which syncs token when messageState is null.

Symptom: Chat list may miss updates on app startup if state events arrive during initial load.

Current code:
  if (changed.Chat && chatState !== null) {
    methodCalls.push(['Chat/changes', ...]);
  }

Should handle chatState === null case symmetrically to messageState.
